
# Conventional Commit Template
#
# Format:
# <type>(<optional-scope>): <short description>
#
# Leave a blank line, then optionally add a multiline body.
# Use the imperative mood: "add", "fix", "update", not "added".
#
# Example:
# feat(auth): add session-based authentication
#
# - Implement session creation and validation
# - Add secure HTTP-only cookies
# - Add authentication tests
#
# -------------------------------
# Commit Types
# -------------------------------
# feat      New feature
# fix       Bug fix
# chore     Maintenance, dependencies, tooling
# docs      Documentation changes
# style     Formatting only (no behavior changes)
# refactor  Code restructuring (no behavior changes)
# test      Add or modify tests
# perf      Performance improvements
# build     Build system or dependency changes
# ci        Continuous integration or deployment
# revert    Revert a previous commit
#
# -------------------------------
# Guidelines
# -------------------------------
# - Keep the subject concise (ideally 50 characters).
# - Do not end the subject with a period.
# - Separate the subject and body with a blank line.
# - Explain what changed and why in the body.
# - Wrap body lines at approximately 72 characters.
# - The scope is optional: feat: ... and feat(auth): ... are valid.
# - All lines beginning with # are comments and won't be committed.